WEBVTT

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.080
Whoa...

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.540
Fool.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.160
Shut up!

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.840
D-Damn it!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.440
Killing is the worst choice you can make.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.250
Of course, so is dying.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.630
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.610
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.490
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:00:58.910 --> 00:00:59.490
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.640
<i>established a clandestine 
spy training agency.</i>

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.040
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.160
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.450
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.810
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.630
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.470
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.310
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.060
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.960
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.760
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:13.080
Episode 10 - Pursuit

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.020
Machiyama-san.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.140
Did you look into the matter 
we discussed yesterday?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.290
This Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki...

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.440
My friend in the Ministry of War says

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.920
there's no record of anyone by that name.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.320
While investigating, he only 
heard about a "D-Agency,"

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.660
the details of which are totally unknown.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.940
Then can you get me the 
Military Prep School's registry

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.620
for the last five years, 
starting from the year 1900?

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.790
For twice the usual, yes.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.400
Fine. I'll send it like always.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:04.840
Machiyama-san, thank you for 
the interesting information.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.640
<i>D-Agency, huh?</i>

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.520
<i>In order to effectively 
use information gathered</i>

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:26.410
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.230
<i>from spies across the globe,</i>

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:28.560
<i>it would be an absolute necessity to have</i>

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.230
<i>a high-ranking commissioned
officer as the spymaster.</i>

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.000
<i>But...</i>

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:38.630
<b>Enrollees</b>

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:38.630
