25 Abe Shouhei / Tokyo, Samurai
26 Matsutake Masashi / Tokyo, Samurai</b>

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:38.630
<b>27 Kubota Kouichi / Tokyo, Commoner 
28 Ishida Daiki / Gunma, Samurai 
29 Andou Mitsuhiro / Ibaraki, Samurai 
30 Nakamura Takanori / Saitama, Samurai 
31 Takahashi Hidetake / Chiba, Samurai
32 Kawaguchi Hideki / Saitama, Samurai 
33 Honda Keisuke / Chiba, Samurai 
34 Maruyama Shouwa / Fukushima, Samurai</b>

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.210
<i>His name is not on the list of graduates.</i>

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.840
Oh, darling? Do you have a moment?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.680
<b>July 1905 

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.110
Come on in, Ellen.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.730
A little something, since 
you're working so hard.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.060
Where's that from?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.440
Our neighbor.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.440
Um...

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.270
Susoake?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.970
"Susoake"?

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:05.520
Oh, that's "o-suso-wake," 
meaning sharing a gift, Ellen.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.220
Oh, right! "O-suso-wake"!

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.730
Here, have some of this and cool off.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:12.790
Thank you.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.460
Oh, dear, it slipped off again.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.090
Try and be more careful, would you?

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.470
That's your wedding ring, after all.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.910
I'm sorry.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.340
Maybe I've lost weight from all this heat?

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.600
Thank you, darling.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.890
You're welcome.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.470
I'll finish the rest while 
I work. You can go to bed.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.330
Okay.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.080
<b>Meiji Year 38, July

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.990
<i>His name wasn't in the list of graduates.</i>

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.270
<i>But...</i>

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:05.760
<b>Enrollee List</b>

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:05.760
<b>123 Aizawa Tomoyoshi / Tokyo, Samurai
124 Arima Aiji / Saitama, Samurai 
125 Arisaki Akira / Tokyo, Samurai 
126 Iijima Jounosuke
127 Izaki Kouhei / Gunma, Samurai
128 Ishikawa Shinichi 
129 Iwakuni Masaemon</b>

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:05.760
<b>130 Uegusa Kouichi / Tokyo 
131 Ugaki Kentarou / Shizuoka, Commoner 
132 Ujioka Toki / Tokyo, Samurai 
133 Uwajima Ken / Ehime, Samurai 
134 Etou Kisaburou / Saitama</b>

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.960
<i>Arisaki Akira.</i>

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:03.150
<i>He's registered as attending the prep school,</i>

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.090
<i>but was expelled for delinquency.</i>

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:12.600
<b>Enrollee List 

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.150
<i>And the characters for "Arisaki" 
can also be read as "Yuuki."</i>

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.060
<b>Satomura</b>

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:19.060
Thanks for coming all this way...

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.020
<b>British Times Newspaper

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.700
Aaron Price-san.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:25.280
Have you been in Japan long?

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.130
Yes. Ten years now.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.830
And before I came here, I was a reporter
in Bombay and Hong Kong.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.630
Ten years, you say?

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:36.200
Your wife is Japanese, then?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.370
Oh, no.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.580
My wife's a Belgian woman 
I met here in Japan.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.950
She's my world.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.200
I see! My apologies.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.630
You were asking about the 
life of Viscount Arisaki?

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:51.680
Yes.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.790
Lately, many of the viscount's close 
friends in England have been

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.500
talking about how dearly they miss him.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.500
Is that so?

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.610
So...

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:05.620
I spoke to some of his former coworkers,

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.320
and I heard an interesting rumor.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:13.320
They said Viscount Arisaki 
had a secret love child.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:18.290
The person you heard about 
was undoubtedly Akira-sama.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:21.470
His name was Akira?

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.900
If he was his child,

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.000
why didn't he inherit the noble rank?

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:30.410
Then the Arisaki line wouldn't have died out.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.250
It was winter of 1896 when Viscount Arisaki

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:40.960
appeared at his manor in Mejiro 
with Akira-sama in tow.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.480
<b>Arisaki</b>

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.690
Welcome home, Master.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.730
Who is this boy?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.740
Draw him a bath, please.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.260
As you wish!

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.620
What is your name?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.160
Akira.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.700
Though he was still young,

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:10.000
the viscount never remarried 
after losing his wife.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.770
He was a tall, athletic, and broad-minded man.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:19.220
And although there were times when
he'd take a cynical view of the world,

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.440
he was extremely popular with women.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.990
So handsome...

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:32.850
Then, suddenly, he returned 
with a young child at his side.

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.650
It was only natural for those near him

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:38.950
to assume he'd fathered him with 
a geisha, or something of the sort.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:43.160
However, after seeing the fortitude

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.500
that gave Akira-sama such a noble air,

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:50.720
rumors that the viscount was just 
caring for an old army comrade's child,

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:53.510
or the illegitimate child of a princess,

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.270
began to seem more plausible.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:09:00.140
In the end, we never learned the truth.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.210
The master never registered Akira-sama

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:06.480
as part of the Arisaki family,

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.970
but we were all shocked by the fervor

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:11.500
with which he educated the boy.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.780
Starting with language:

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:16.700
not just English, but French,

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.210
German, Russian, and Chinese, as well.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.890
Math, history, physics, and chemistry.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:27.200
He had tutors of different races 
from all over the world.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:31.410
And to top it all off, the master himself

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:34.170
taught the boy martial arts.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:43.890
In deadly training sessions where a 
single misstep could cost him his life,

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:50.550
the master beat his lessons into 
Akira-sama with a fury that only a man

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:53.650
who'd risked his life on a real 
battlefield could muster.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:00.140
And with Akira-sama's unbelievable
aptitude for learning,

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:02.370
he absorbed everything he was taught.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:07.140
Then, when he was 13, 
Akira-sama applied to

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.960
the Military Preparatory School 
at the Master's behest.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.970
He scored the highest grade 
of all the applicants.

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:16.670
Wow, that's impressive.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:22.600
Yes. I thought for sure he'd 
end up a decorated soldier,

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.320
until there was an incident...

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.560
<b>Principal's Office</b>

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.240
Why is Akira-sama the only 
one being expelled?!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:34.450
This is about having the 
temperament of a soldier.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.490
They're just boys. Fights aren't a problem.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.100
Sometimes a scuffle is the 
start of a new friendship,

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.220
as long as they fight fair and square.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.410
But blinding the opponent with dirt

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.240
and hitting him with a low blow

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.790
is nothing but cowardice!

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.660
It's unbecoming of a soldier.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.360
My school's job is to raise soldiers.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.550
A boy with cowardice in his heart

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.790
isn't fit to be a student here!

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.770
Akira-sama.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.910
Do you still have the knife I gave to you?

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:18.280
Of course.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.950
Why didn't you use it when 
you were surrounded?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:29.630
When they gather together, 
they stop being afraid of death.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.660
It's one of the things they 
teach at that school.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.930
If I'd used my knife,

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.340
someone would have died.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:42.840
What did Akira-san do after being expelled?

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.320
He studied abroad in England

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.240
and remained there.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.370
No returns to Japan?

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:53.350
Just once, in 1912...

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.860
for Viscount Arisaki's funeral.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.240
Akira-sama had grown into a fine gentleman,

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:05.200
and attracted the attention of women, 
whether he wanted to or not.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:12.330
After the funeral, Akira-sama

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.380
sold off the manor in accordance 
with the viscount's wishes,

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:20.610
and left most of the money to the servants.

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.260
But the man himself took nothing.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.470
Old man. Thanks for everything.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.460
Are you leaving Japan again?

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:33.930
Yeah. I'm boarding a boat 
back to Europe tonight.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.110
If I may be so bold,

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.970
is there no way I can assist you?

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.660
Old man, I've advanced quite far out there.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.200
Don't worry.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.020
Everyone around here

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:51.300
is calling me "Duke."

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:54.300
Duke?!

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.720
<i>Duke... The title of Duke...</i>

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:01.120
<i>The first letter is "D."</i>

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:05.220
The young man here in the upper right corner

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.800
is Akira-sama after he'd just 
begun studying in England.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.130
Who's this?

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:13.220
I'm told he acted as

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:16.470
Akira-sama's guardian during his time there.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.490
<i>Arisaki Akira left to study in England</i>

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.120
<i>in 1906.</i>

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.640
<i>Britain's security service became</i>

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:32.440
<i>an independent secret 
intelligence service in 1909.</i>

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.320
<i>When the era of MI6 began,</i>

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:38.690
<i>was there, or was there not, an Asian 
man who could be Akira enrolled there?</i>

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.460
<i>That's the only thing left to confirm.</i>

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.840
<i>How ironic, though...</i>

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:47.970
<i>Arisaki Akira was taught by none other</i>

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.910
<i>than Captain Mansfield 
Cumming of the Royal Navy.</i>

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:53.690
<i>One of the creators of MI6,</i>

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.850
<i>and a legendary English spymaster.</i>

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.100
<i>That makes Arisaki</i>

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.020
<i>a senior apprentice to me.</i>

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.820
<i>The Japanese spy who was 
captured by, and escaped from,</i>

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.360
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Marks was from D-Agency.</i>

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.330
<i>Which is run by</i>

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:13.860
<i>Imperial Army Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki.</i>

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.540
<i>That much I already knew.</i>

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:21.960
<i>"A dog is more useful than 
a spy whose cover is blown."</i>

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.710
<i>Captain Cumming said that a lot.</i>

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:34.930
Aaron Price.

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.650
You're under arrest for espionage.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.320
<i>Why did this happen?</i>

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.000
How long are you gonna keep playing dumb?

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.830
We caught you red-handed. 
You can't talk your way out of this.

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:08.980
If you won't cooperate,

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.390
we'll just ask your wife Ellen.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.490
Ellen has nothing to do with this!

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:17.340
You're clearly in possession 
of military secrets.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:19.060
You'll get the death penalty for sure.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.060
Who are you working with?

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.440
Who are you working with?!

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:28.680
<i>Why...</i>

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.000
Could I have a cigarette?

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:40.370
I give up. I'll tell you everything.

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:55.550
<i>Ellen,</i>

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:58.470
<i>what I've put you through is unforgivable.</i>

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.220
<i>I wish that, just once more...</i>

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:18.760
Release him.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.120
Take off the handcuffs.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:35.440
<i>Why? Why did they let me go?</i>

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:37.930
<i>The MP was right.</i>

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.930
<i>They caught me red-handed and 
had all the proof they needed.</i>

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:44.310
<i>I had no possible room for excuses,</i>

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.640
<i>so to save my own life...</i>

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:51.280
<i>The MPs timed it perfectly, too.</i>

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.210
<i>Did Machiyama...</i>

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:54.750
<i>No, it couldn't be.</i>

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.070
<i>Then...</i>

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.980
<i>It had to be the next person I met...</i>

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.800
Satomura-san.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:14.260
Price-san? What on earth are you doing here?

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.020
Where is Arisaki Akira?

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.030
This is Akira-sama.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:34.940
<i>Impossible...</i>

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.720
<i>This is him?!</i>

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.750
<i>Arisaki Akira...</i>

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.930
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki... runs D-Agency...</i>

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:47.790
Akira-sama has been sleeping 
like this for over 20 years.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:51.740
In the world war, he served 
as a volunteer soldier.

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:53.800
During the Battle of Passchendaele,

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.020
he was caught in a German
gas bombardment.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:59.790
After he was transferred back to Japan,

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:03.090
we requested medical help 
from the Imperial Army,

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:08.020
but they refused, saying 
he wasn't an imperial soldier.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:13.190
As we found ourselves completely 
at a loss, a man came.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.350
He said that he and

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:21.370
Akira-sama had been close friends in Europe.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:24.910
That man pays for all this?

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.250
But why?

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.920
I don't know the real reason, either.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:35.160
He had conditions, however.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:36.550
Conditions?

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.960
First, that I not ask his name.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.800
The other...

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:46.270
was teaching me exactly what 
to say when, in the future,

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:49.770
someone came by asking about Akira-sama.

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:52.620
Akira-sama's new past.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:58.510
I've repeated it to myself over and over,

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.990
memorizing it in minute detail.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:04.740
At this point, I can't even distinguish

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:07.820
which parts really happened to Akira-sama.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.630
Nonetheless,

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:13.710
I was thrilled when you came to see me.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:18.820
I thought that the world had 
forgotten about Akira-sama.

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:23.170
<i>Yuuki fabricated a whole past for himself</i>

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.740
<i>as bait to lure out enemy spies?</i>

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.090
<i>But... then...</i>

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:31.690
<i>Why let me go?!</i>

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.400
Price-sama...

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.970
Where's your ring?

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.280
<i>They got me.</i>

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.430
<i>At that point,</i>

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:46.210
<i>they knew nothing about my spy network.</i>

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:50.180
<i>If they'd even implied they 
knew anything, I'd have...</i>

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:57.090
<i>They must've been Yuuki's subordinates.</i>

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:01.210
<i>That ring contained</i>

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:04.810
<i>a microdot list of the 
informants and accomplices</i>

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.560
<i>that I've spent ten years in Japan compiling!</i>

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:33.690
<i>Ten years I've been in this country...</i>

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.560
<i>Everything I've accomplished 
in that time is gone.</i>

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:41.470
<i>A decade of my life...</i>

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:51.270
Ellen...

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:55.970
Dear.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.430
How did you know?

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:08.480
A man with a cane

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.580
told me you'd be here.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:18.040
I'm sorry.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.410
Darling...

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:26.180
Let's go home.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:32.940
<i>"When a spy is at a crossroads, if their 
partner's face comes to mind first,</i>

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:34.970
<i>it's time for them to retire."</i>

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:38.150
<i>That's a famous saying among spies.</i>

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:46.970
Thank you.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.000
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.210
Millais's "Ophelia."

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:28.850
Is she still alive,

00:23:29.210 --> 00:23:30.470
or dead?

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 11 - Coffin

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:34.430
What do you think?
